` THE REROLL. next to the line that takes nothing there is a line that throws the cards away and deals
` new ones, for a price in moves, which are added to the count of moves. the first time on an upgrade
` screen costs UPGRADE_REROLL_STEP moves, and every time after that costs that much more than the
` last, up to UPGRADE_REROLL_MAX times. the next upgrade screen starts from the first price again.
` the new cards are not the ones that were thrown away, as long as there are others to deal.
` down goes from the cards to these two lines, left and right go between them, and up goes back.
global UPGRADE_REROLL_STEP = 5
global UPGRADE_REROLL_MAX = 4
