global UPGRADE_REROLL_TEXT_ID
global UPGRADE_REROLL_X = 0 `where the middle of the line is. setup_upgrade_wipe works it out.
global dim CARD_CHOICE_OLD(10) `the cards that are being thrown away

` DROPPING A PASSIVE. the third line under the cards, to the right of the one that takes nothing, gives a
` passive up, and that is what the player gets from the upgrade screen that time: no card is taken.
` it opens a page that lists the passives that are owned, with what the highlighted one does written
` above them, and a row at the end that goes back to the cards. picking a passive asks if the player
` is sure, and "yes" is the far answer, the same as when a move is left behind.
` a passive that is dropped is gone, every copy of it, as if it had never been taken. an upgrade can
` offer it again. the passives under it in the list at the side of the board move up a row.
` dropping "bottom feeder" drops its second copy too, which is nothing without it. and in a zen game
` "seamless" is not on the list, because the game is given it, and is not the same game without it.
` when no passive is owned, the line is dim, and picking it does nothing.
` the page is in fish_routines_drop, and so is dropPassive, which does the dropping.
global UPGRADE_DROP_TEXT_ID
