` THE KIND OF GAME. "New Game" on the menu asks how long the game should be, and which mode it is in.
` the length is how many rounds there are. when the last one has been won, the game is over.
` the mode is normal or zen. a zen game starts with the "seamless" passive, and that is all that it
` ever gets: there is no upgrade screen. when the bar fills up, it empties out and the next round starts.
` the menu changes the two options, and they are remembered for the next time the game is run. they only
` turn into the rules of a game when one is started. apply_game_options, in fish_routines_menu, does that.
#constant GAME_LENGTH_SHORT 0
#constant GAME_LENGTH_REGULAR 1
#constant GAME_LENGTH_LONG 2
global OPTION_GAME_LENGTH = 1
global OPTION_GAME_ZEN = 0
global GAME_ROUND_CAP = 100 `how many rounds the game that is being played has
global GAME_ZEN = 0 `1 when the game that is being played is a zen game

` KEEP PLAYING. this is not offered any more: a game that is won ends with the fish going home, and
` that is the end of it. see THE FISH GO HOME. the rest of this is how it worked, and the page and its
` lines are still there.
` when the last round has been won, and the game has been put on its table, the player
` can carry on with the same board, for as long as they like. the game has been counted already, so it
` is never counted again: no round is the last one any more, and the rounds that are played from then
` on are shown as "+1", "+2", and so on, where the rounds that were left used to be. it is saved with
` the game. a game that ended with one of the two endings of the hidden game cannot be carried on
` with, and one of those endings in a game that is being carried on goes straight back to the title.
global GAME_ENDLESS = 0 `1 when the game that is being played was won, and is being carried on with
global REQUEST_GAME_END = 0 `1 when the last round has been won, and the end of the game has not come up yet

` THE FISH GO HOME. a game that is won the usual way, by getting through its rounds, ends with the fish
` leaving. the cursor fades away, and the fish swim off of the board, slowly, to the right, the ones
` nearest to that side first, fanning out a little as they go. the words come up over that: "The fish
` need to go home, now. Bye bye!", and then, a moment later and smaller, "If they had a home...".
` a fish that is sitting on coral that is well has one, and does not go anywhere: it stays in its cell,
` and is still there under the end of the game. a fish on horror coral leaves with the rest.
` and while they go, everything around the board that was about playing fades away: the bar of the round,
` which was full and fizzing, and the rounds that were left, the bar of the multiplier, the passives and
` the special moves, the songs and their bars, and the key hints. what is left is the count of moves, and
` the multiplier: the score. HUD_KEEP# is how much of the rest is still there, and applyHudFade, in
` fish_routines_coral, is what fades it, at the end of every frame, after everything has been drawn the
` way that it usually is.
` then the end of the game comes up as it always did, over an empty board, and after the table of high
` scores it is back to the title. a game that ended this way is over, and cannot be carried on with.
` finale_goodbye, in fish_routines_coral, plays it, and it borrows the words and the lists of the two
` endings of the hidden game. see THE TWO ENDINGS.
global GOODBYE_SPEED# = 46 `how fast a fish swims off, in pixels a second, give or take
global GOODBYE_STAGGER_MS = 260 `how much later each column sets off than the one to the right of it, in milliseconds
global GOODBYE_SUB_MS = 1500 `how long after the first words the smaller ones start to come up
global GOODBYE_MAX_MS = 13000 `how long it lasts, if the player does not move it on
global FISH_AWAY = 0 `1 while the fish have left the board, and have not been put back. see fishComeHome.
global GOODBYE_HUD_MS = 1400 `how long the things around the board take to fade away
global HUD_KEEP# = 1 `how much of the things around the board is there, from 1 (all of it, as always) to 0 (none)

global OPTION_SOUND = 10 `how loud the sound effects are, from 0 to 10
global OPTION_MUSIC = 10 `how loud the music is, from 0 to 10
global OPTION_FULLSCREEN = 0

` how big the window was before the game filled the screen, so that it can go back to that size afterwards.
` the player sets the size of the window by dragging its edges.
global OPTION_WINDOW_W = 0
global OPTION_WINDOW_H = 0

` THE SURFACE. the main menu is the view from the surface of the water. the routines are in fish_routines_surface.
