` THE LOG OF UPGRADES. every upgrade that gets picked is written down, with the move that it was picked on.
` each one is one number: the move, times 100, plus the card. logUpgrade, in fish_routines_highscores, adds one.
` the log of the game that is being played is saved with the game. when a game gets onto a table, its log
` goes with it, and picking its row on the table shows it.
global HISCORE_LOG_MAX = 100 `the most upgrades that get written down for one game

` THE QUESTS IN THE LOG. the log also says which quest was finished in every round, if one was. an
` upgrade is picked at the end of every round but the last, so the upgrade that is logged for a
` round carries the quest that was finished in that round: its number in the log is the quest,
` times LOG_QUEST_STEP, on top of the move and the card. LOG_QUEST_STEP is a round number that is
` bigger than any move times 100, so the move and the card read the same as ever once it is taken
` off, and a log from before there were quests has no quest in it. the last round of a game has no
` upgrade to carry its quest, so that one is kept with the count of the log: the first number of a
` log is how many upgrades there are, plus LOG_LAST_STEP times the quest of the last round.
` logMoveOf, logQuestOf, logCountOf and logLastQuestOf, in fish_routines_highscores, take them apart.
` QUEST_LOG_PENDING, in fish_headers_quests, is the quest that has been finished since the last upgrade.
global LOG_QUEST_STEP = 50000000
global LOG_LAST_STEP = 1000
global GAME_LOG_COUNT = 0
global dim GAME_LOG(100)

` the log of every entry on every table. each entry has HISCORE_LOG_STRIDE numbers: how many upgrades
` there are, and then the upgrades. entry n starts at n * HISCORE_LOG_STRIDE.
global HISCORE_LOG_STRIDE = 101
global dim HISCORE_LOGS(5656)

` where the logs are kept in the preferences. a table has 1000 numbers, and they must not move.
global HISCORE_LOG_PREF = 10000
global SAVE_PREF_LOG = 500 `and where the log of the saved game is kept, with the rest of the saved game

