` THE QUESTS ON STEAM. the quests that were finished go in the bits right after the log of upgrades,
` which nothing else uses, and which a game from before there were quests never looks at: it reads
` as many upgrades as the count says, and stops. so the way that a score is packed has not changed,
` STEAM_PACK_VERSION is still 1, and an old game shows a new score the same as any other.
` for every upgrade of the log, in order, there is one bit: 1 if a quest was finished in that round.
` when it is 1, the next STEAM_QUEST_BITS bits are the quest, less one. after the last upgrade come
` STEAM_QUEST_BITS + 1 bits for the quest of the last round, which has no upgrade: the quest, or 0.
` detail 5 is STEAM_QUEST_TAG, plus 256 times how many upgrades have their bit, plus 65536 if the
` quest of the last round is there. a long game has 60 rounds, so its log is 1080 bits at the very
` most, and its quests 366, out of the 1856 that there are. they always fit. a game that was saved
` when a long game had 100 rounds could run out, and then only as many as fit are written.
global STEAM_QUEST_TAG = 1
global STEAM_QUEST_BITS = 5
global STEAM_BITS_TOTAL = 2048 `a score has 64 details of 32 bits
global STEAM_GLOBAL_FETCH = 40 `how many of everybody's scores are asked for, to find 8 that pass their check

