` THE OPENING SWAP. players kept walking patterns by accident, so a song is now all of the steps between
` two swaps, and nothing else: a swap, then the pattern, step for step, then a swap that pops. a walk
` that only ends with the pattern does not count. the start of a game counts as the opening swap.
` and a pattern has to double back on itself: somewhere in it there is a step one way, and a step the
` other way. nobody walks like that to get from one fish to another.
`
` two cards bend the rule. neither is offered until CORAL_SONG_CARDS_AFTER patterns have been cast in
` the game, which is all of the first ones, so they only come to a player who has found the hidden game.
`   "quick song", a passive: no opening swap. a walk that ends with the pattern counts, the way it used to.
`   "easy song", a move: it opens a song right where the cursor is, and takes the first step of it. the
`       pattern is walked step for step from there, and it is cast on its last step, with no swap at all,
`       and nothing has to pop. a step that is not of any pattern loses it, and so does a swap.
`       the outline of the cursor is the color of coral while a song is open.
global CORAL_DOUBLE_BACK = 1 `1 if every pattern has to double back on itself
global CORAL_SONG_CARDS_AFTER = 3 `how many patterns have to be cast in a game before the two cards are offered
global CORAL_SONG_COOLDOWN = 8 `how many moves "easy song" takes to be ready again
global CORAL_TRAIL_TOTAL = 0 `how many steps the cursor has taken since the last swap, or since "easy song" opened a song
#constant CORAL_TRAIL_SPOILED 99
global CORAL_OPEN = 0 `1 while a song that "easy song" opened is being walked
` the opening swap takes the cursor one step along with it, and that step can be the first step of
` the pattern, or not, as the player likes. starting a pattern from where a swap left the cursor was
` too hard to line up. the closing swap is still not a step.
global CORAL_TRAIL_SWAP_FIRST = 0 `1 while the first step since the last swap is the step of that swap

` a hint brings out a few more specks where it is, and they drift the way that it is going. this is how
` far they have drifted, in pixels. it only ever adds up, so that they do not jump when it turns.
global CORAL_HINT_FLOW# = 16 `how fast they drift, in pixels a second
global CORAL_HINT_FLOW_X# = 0
global CORAL_HINT_FLOW_Y# = 0
global CORAL_HINT_FLOW_MS = 0 `when it was last added to

` the last steps that the cursor took on its own, oldest first, and the cell that each one started from
global CORAL_TRAIL_COUNT = 0
global dim CORAL_TRAIL_DIR(CORAL_STEP_MAX)
global dim CORAL_TRAIL_X(CORAL_STEP_MAX)
global dim CORAL_TRAIL_Y(CORAL_STEP_MAX)

