` THE HINTS. now and then something small goes along the shape of a pattern that is out, somewhere on the
` board: a couple of bubbles come up from the cell at one end of it, then a patch of the water goes calm,
` and the calm moves slowly from cell to cell along the pattern, and a couple more bubbles come up from the
` cell at the other end. all of the water wobbles all of the time, and has ripples of light in it. in the
` patch it is still and clear. and the specks that are drifting behind the board anyway glow as they
` pass through where it is. the screen effect does the calm, and the specks effect does the specks.
` over coral the water hardly moves, so there is no calm to see, and the specks are lost against the rock.
` so there, the specks glow a lot more, and the coral itself lights up where the hint is passing: the
` rock, and the things that grow on it. the coral effect does that.
` it is meant to be easy to miss, and hard to miss once it has been noticed.
` which pattern it is, where on the board, and which end it starts from, is picked at random every time.
` none of those matter. only the shape does, because a pattern can be walked from either end.
` it happens on its own every so often: when a wave of the current sets out, there is a chance of one. and
` a big group of fish that pops always brings one, as soon as the board has settled.

` LISTEN. with the "listen" card, a hint is a lot easier to see. the specks glow brighter, and further out
` from where it is, and it leaves a trail of light behind it, along the path that it took, which fades
` and thins the further back it is, and bends where it turned. CORAL_HINT_TRAIL# is the path, for the specks
` effect to draw it. a hint that a big group of fish brought always leaves a trail, and a hint that
` came on its own does CORAL_LISTEN_LUCK times in a hundred, and that is when the name of the card shakes
` in the list of passives. see CORAL_HINT_TRAIL_ON. the
` patch of calm water is bigger. more bubbles come up at each end. and the name of the card shakes in
` the list of passives when a hint starts. it does not make hints come any more often.
` SHOW TIME. an instant card. the next SHOW_TIME_HINTS hints, however they come about, are the kind that a
` big group of fish brings with the "listen" card: bright, with more bubbles, and with the trail of light
` behind them. it does not take the "listen" card to see them, and it does not make hints come any sooner.
` taking it again adds that many more. coralRollHint, in fish_routines_coral, counts them down.
global SHOW_TIME_HINTS = 2
